1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:06,408
In 218 BC, Hannibal set out from Spain to attack Rome.

2
00:00:06,208 --> 00:00:09,878
Rome ruled the sea. So he went by land.

3
00:00:09,778 --> 00:00:14,004
Over the Pyrenees, with about 59,000 men.

4
00:00:13,904 --> 00:00:18,500
He crossed the Rhône, ferrying his elephants over on rafts.

5
00:00:18,580 --> 00:00:20,688
Then came the Alps.

6
00:00:20,488 --> 00:00:24,866
Snow, landslides, and attacks from mountain tribes.

7
00:00:24,666 --> 00:00:28,556
Which pass he used is still argued over today.

8
00:00:28,356 --> 00:00:31,024
The crossing took 15 days.

9
00:00:31,104 --> 00:00:35,579
He came down into Italy with about 26,000 men.

10
00:00:35,479 --> 00:00:39,220
Fewer than half the men who crossed the Pyrenees.

11
00:00:39,220 --> 00:00:44,087
And with them, he fought in Italy for 15 years.
